{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/840767-dragon-blooded-artifact-production","id":840767,"title":"Dragon-Blooded Artifact Production","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Dragon-Blooded"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-02T10:46:14-08:00","id":840767,"title":"Dragon-Blooded Artifact Production","content":"So from my understanding Dragon-Blooded now use a generational mechanic for Evocations which makes the length of a lineage relevant to the power of the Evocations. I am rather curious as to the repercussions of this and what they mean for the Realm. How does this affect the Realm's weapon production? Would it mean that the Realm has less need of MM than previous editions? And what does this mean for Outcaste's? Does a skipped generation mean that you loose all your family's efforts? And will you now have to consider mass-fratricide to get your hands on your families neatest toy? Would Lookshy's ancient families have a huge advantage?<br /> From my understanding this means that the Realm would only really need to produce artifacts for Outcastes, poorly-bred dynasts and replacements for really unlucky dynasts. Does that mean that if two Terrestrials of equal skill and experience and breeding fight, their family history with their weapon decides the outcome? <br /> <br /> Just a few questions that i would like to hear some theories about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T11:15:54-08:00","id":840790,"title":"","content":"I don't think this is more than speculation or one way that it might be done, not a general rule.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T14:43:39-08:00","id":840927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/840767-dragon-blooded-artifact-production?p=840790#post840790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think this is more than speculation or one way that it might be done, not a general rule.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I figured since the books that will explain all of this are months away at best and so it would be interesting to speculate on how this idea would affect the Realm and Dragon-Blooded in general.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T15:30:04-08:00","id":840947,"title":"","content":"First on the part of whether not the idea of DBs needing generations to cultivate evocations* would reduce the need to the magic materials. Not so much. I mean first an artifact weapon or armor is still going to be extremely resilient and useful for exalts, so you'll still have Jade diaklaves being viewed as superior to a steel one. Not to mention the artistic merit and craftsmanship that goes into an artifact will invariably put it down as an amazing object even if one never tries to bond with the sword to gain it's powers.<br /> <br /> On the matter of outcastes and such no I'm not seeing the realm being too big on handing out weapons of superior quality to people who don't have allegience to the realm ,ie whichever family might be handing over the weapon. Not to mention a growing population in most of the realm and the great houses would make it a fair case to argue for the creation/discovery/recovery of &quot;new&quot; artifacts to better bolster a family's arsenal and better protect the family and it's charges.<br /> <br /> As for generation things remember the families probably aren't knowingly cultivating evocations. Hell it's entirely possible and reasonable to wield an artifact weapon like spring razor and never find out about it's powers. So evocations on a weapon might show up less as &quot;and once you have bonded with the blade it will let electrocute your enemies on contact&quot; and more &quot;there's a story in my family about how Honorable Shen was so fast and struck so hard with this blade that his enemies often dropped like they'd been struck by lightning, in his honor it's only passed down to the best swordsman in the family when the previous bearer passes on.&quot; <br /> <br /> Plus as I understand evocations are more like a psuedomystical manifestation of the artifacts history.(Partially why they show up more on weapons and armor than jewelry.) So it isn't like all that goes away just because no one wields it for a generation. I mean to use one from the book Black Wind was originally used to hunt down and kill murderers, traitors, and the like. Then after it lost its original wielder it was used by assassins until 110 years ago when its wielder sealed it away because he became convinced the Black Wind wanted him dead. If a single generation of no one using an artifact wiped away its evocations than the Black Wind should have reconfigured its powers towards being the tool of an assassin instead of it's focus on killing murderers. <br /> <br /> I will also point out the last bit. Bullet point the second on evocation rules: Artifacts are generally designed to synchronize with certain essence types and very few will offer up their power to any wielder. So basically an artifact created with it in mind that it would be wielded by DBs will probably have evocations that DBs can use without having to wait and hope that the weapon will develop the powers needed in time for the great great grandchild of the current house leader and really hope they actually use that kind of weapon. Cause lets face it you probably aren't focusing too much on using your families battle gauntlets in a fight if your preferred combat method is shoot it in the face from far away.<br /> <br /> <br /> * I doubt DBs will require generations to get access to evocations on a blade though. I mean a generational blade might eventually pick up evocations from the family, but nothing saying it might not have some good tricks to start with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T15:50:28-08:00","id":840956,"title":"","content":"I'd probably prefer DB evocations to be either family lineage or deeply personal to the user. <br /> <br /> It seems weird for a DB to have gained or crafted a tool which is very personal to them, for it to be necessarily weaker than one which has been in the blood for a long time.<br /> <br /> At the same time, yeah, I can see sure, the family heirlooms of others may not sing as well for you. Possibly this means DBs do lots of complicated trades for their ancestors' weapons...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}